# Use Strategic Thinking to Create the Life You Want

![rw-book-cover](https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2023/12/lifestrategy_strack_feature.jpg)

## Metadata
- Author: [[Rainer Strack,
Susanne Dyrchs,
Allison Bailey]]
- Full Title: Use Strategic Thinking to Create the Life You Want
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: The article discusses the importance of creating a life strategy to navigate life's transitions and difficult moments while building resilience and finding joy and fulfillment. The authors provide a seven-step process for developing an individual life strategy, including defining what a great life means, outlining one's purpose and vision, assessing one's life portfolio, and setting priorities and making commitments. To develop a job/career strategy, one should consider how their current job supports their purpose and vision, their sense of achievement and engagement, and their identified strengths. The article emphasizes the importance of finding one's own path and making sustained life changes through strategic thinking.
- URL: https://hbr.org/2023/12/use-strategic-thinking-to-create-the-life-you-want/

## Highlights
- Just as corporate strategy is an integrated set of choices that positions a company to win, *life strategy* is an integrated set of choices *that positions a person to live a great life* ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hj5cfn248hm7xvrt9mnw182f))
- What are the right metrics in an individual’s life? Our social norms and hierarchies might suggest we measure ourselves with money, fame, and power. But [studies have shown](https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.1011492107) that money leads to greater happiness only to the extent that our basic needs are met, after which its returns diminish or even plateau ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hj5cmmmw1n1pqm9esy9nzfm3))
- The ancient Greeks saw two main dimensions of a great life: *hedonia* (a focus on pleasure) and *eudaimonia* (a focus on virtues and on meaning) ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hj5cnnd4jq38eej81yx7d4fk))
- PERMA-V, which stands for Positive emotions (frequent feelings of pleasure and contentment), Engagement (being in the flow, losing track of time), Relationships (mutual feelings of caring, support, and love), Meaning (contributing to making the world a better place), Achievement (striving for success or mastery, reaching goals), and Vitality (being healthy and energetic). ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hj5cpvvts6bhdy5zbb308hj4))


